{
  "about": "Every route of the operations view and how the public tablet demo answers it (#892, B1). The demo runs in the visitor's browser with no server behind it, so each request the real pages make must be answered here. api/tests/test_tablet_demo_routes.py fails when the view gains a route, a template or the TypeScript names a /gui target, or a route moves behind the owner's PIN, without this file saying how the demo answers it.",
  "answers": {
    "page": "A whole page, rendered by scripts/demo/tablet_demo_build.py from the real templates with the invented data; links to it lead to the static file.",
    "fragment": "An answer rendered by the build, the same for every visitor (per id where the route has one); the fake backend (B2) serves the captured file.",
    "state": "Answered by the fake backend from the visitor's own state (B2 board, B3 sheets and pages, B4 floor plan). A GET of this kind is captured once as the starting state.",
    "locked": "Behind the owner's PIN in the real view: shown, not usable, with the note \"In der echten Version mit Inhaber-PIN\" (B3).",
    "absent": "Not part of the demo: no page of the demo may name it."
  },
  "routes": [
